# /work/ELK is a 3.7 GB runtime tree: downloaded Elastic distributions, indexed
# data, CDR exports, registries and logs. None of that belongs in version control.
#
# Strategy: ignore everything, then re-include only the hand-written configuration.
# Git will not descend into an ignored directory, so each level has to be
# un-ignored before its contents can be selected.

/*

!.gitignore
!README.md
!start-elk.sh
!systemd/
!index-templates/

# --- Logstash pipeline ---
!logstash-9.3.0/
logstash-9.3.0/*
!logstash-9.3.0/config/
logstash-9.3.0/config/*
!logstash-9.3.0/config/logstash-cdrs.conf

# --- Filebeat shipper ---
!filebeat-9.3.0-linux-x86_64/
filebeat-9.3.0-linux-x86_64/*
!filebeat-9.3.0-linux-x86_64/filebeat-cdrs.yml

# --- Never commit, regardless of the rules above ---
.elk-env
*.keystore
**/logstash.keystore
**/elasticsearch.keystore
*.out
*.log
